        "original_id": "2ec19f28-910d-51ba-9b64-f0da69a1689f",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Xavier Malisse, Gene Mayer, Ruben Bemelmans, Jamie Delgado, Ken Skupski\n- Events: 2012 Farmers Classic – Doubles, 1982 Bavarian Tennis Championships\n- Topics: tennis, singles titles, doubles title defense\n\nFacts:\n- Gene Mayer was born on April 11, 1956, and is a former tennis player from the United States.\n- Xavier Malisse was born on July 19, 1980, and is a Belgian retired professional tennis player.\n- Gene Mayer won the singles title at the 1982 Bavarian Tennis Championships.\n- Gene Mayer won 14 singles titles during his career.\n- At the 2012 Farmers Classic – Doubles, Xavier Malisse and fellow Belgian Ruben Bemelmans defended the title.\n- In the final of the 2012 Farmers Classic – Doubles, Xavier Malisse and Ruben Bemelmans defeated Jamie Delgado and Ken Skupski 7–6, 4–6, [10–7].",
